      "id": 1,
      "text": "Southgate was incorporated on October 8, 1958, emerging from the former Ecorse Township.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        17
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Southgate%2C_Michigan",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The city’s name, “Southgate,” reflects its position south of Detroit, serving as the Metro Detroit entrance.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4,
        23
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Southgate%2C_Michigan",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "After WWII, Southgate evolved from rural farmlands to a modern residential hub, with street grids laid in the 1920s.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1,
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Southgate%2C_Michigan",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Southgate Arena and an extensive park network, plus a civic center built in 1976, are key community assets.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/Southgate,_Michigan",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Four SMART bus routes run through Southgate, connecting residents to the wider Downriver region.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
